{%- comment -%}
  The aurora band — port of components/ui/aurora.tsx.

  A slow gradient wash for low-density bands with no photography — the bag
  summary and the footer. The technique is two CSS classes (.wl-aurora in
  base.css) with the stop list in tokens.css, so it recolours with the palette
  instead of carrying colours of its own.

  `tone` HAS to match the surface underneath: the veil layer is painted in the
  surface colour, and a mismatch shows up as a visible rectangle. That is the
  bug this effect always has.

  Never place it behind photography or the logotype — the clear-space and
  contrast rules in the design system apply to whatever sits on top.

  The parent must carry `relative isolate overflow-hidden`. `isolate` is not
  optional: it is what keeps soft-light blending against the band rather than
  against the page. And never wrap the parent in anything that animates opacity
  — that makes the wrapper a stacking context and draws a visible rectangle.

  Accepts: tone ('canvas' | 'muted' | 'inert' | 'invert'),
           origin ('bottom-left' | 'top-right' | 'top-left'),
           intensity (0-1), class
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  case tone
    when 'invert'
      assign veil = 'var(--wl-taupe-900)'
      assign stops = 'var(--wl-aurora-stops-invert)'
    when 'muted'
      assign veil = 'var(--wl-taupe-100)'
      assign stops = 'var(--wl-aurora-stops)'
    when 'inert'
      assign veil = 'var(--wl-inert-100)'
      assign stops = 'var(--wl-aurora-stops)'
    else
      assign veil = 'var(--wl-cream)'
      assign stops = 'var(--wl-aurora-stops)'
  endcase

  case origin
    when 'top-right'
      assign origin_position = '100% 0%'
    when 'top-left'
      assign origin_position = '20% 0%'
    else
      assign origin_position = '0% 100%'
  endcase

  assign aurora_intensity = intensity | default: 1
-%}

<div
  aria-hidden="true"
  class="wl-aurora {{ class }}"
  style="opacity:{{ aurora_intensity }};--aurora-veil:{{ veil }};--aurora-stops:{{ stops }};--aurora-origin:{{ origin_position }}"
></div>
